      "id": "SHELL-MESH-DIRECT-ADJACENCY-ENDPOINT-95E",
      "status": "source-level conditional direct-public-call admission question; central reconciliation of uniqueness/policy pending",
      "condition": "A caller supplies a public ShellMesh whose edge or seam endpoint is at least positions.len(), then directly calls adjacency without successfully validating it. No such application caller or runtime panic was observed.",
      "trace": "ShellMesh.adjacency concatenates its public edge and seam lists then calls SelfCollision.adjacency with the positions count; that helper allocates exactly one list per position and indexes both endpoints without a local bounds check. Rust indexing would fail for an out-of-range endpoint. The canonical Shell::new calls mesh.validate before mesh.adjacency, so this hypothetical is not admitted through the selected constructor path.",
      "relationships": "059 q622 already leaves self-collision adjacency membership open; q3296 concerns topology input/index and density; 774 F083 concerns independently mutable retained Shell state. These are connected but not assumed identical; no duplicate count.",
      "future_repair_direction": "Decide the public direct-call contract: admit/check endpoint membership before indexing or expose adjacency only through an already validated mesh state. Preserve valid seam and edge semantics and keep canonical Shell constructor validation.",
