    {
      "id": "SHELL-MATERIAL-THICKNESS-RECIPROCAL-95E",
      "status": "conditional current-source continuation of 774/059 underflow observation; supported-scale and unique-count policy open",
      "condition": "A caller supplies a smallest positive binary32 subnormal thickness, Shell::new succeeds through its other operations, and a self-collision record is enabled with at least two particles and within capacity. No Shell, float operation, GPU, simulation or fixture was run.",
      "trace": "ShellMaterial.validate accepts finite thickness >0. Under IEEE binary32 round-to-nearest, half of 2^-149 rounds to zero; particle_radius therefore may become zero even though the thickness passed. SelfCollision::new stores radius and spacing=2*radius. The selected record path computes 1/spacing, producing positive infinity for zero spacing, inserts that value as inverse_spacing and requests a hash dispatch. WGSL source multiplies positions by inverse_spacing before floor and integer conversion; its actual device result and impact are not established.",
      "relationships": "Original rig ADD103 and 059 L11-433 already noted positive-thickness halving can underflow; this independently traces current downstream reciprocal and intended native port. Existing SHELL-SELF-COLLISION-FIXED-POINT-QUANTIZATION concerns a distinct correction quantization at a less extreme scale; SHELL-GRID-RADIUS-SPACING-DIVERGENCE concerns independent mutation of radius versus spacing. Do not automatically merge or increase unique counts.",
      "future_repair_direction": "Decide supported physical scale and zero-radius policy, then admit a usable positive finite derived radius/spacing/reciprocal before the consumer or explicitly represent disabled contact when intended. Preserve ordinary valid material and legitimate intentional zero-contact modes; validation is deferred.",
