  "open_questions": [
    "Should public ShellMesh::adjacency and SelfCollision::adjacency accept arbitrary raw arrays with recoverable error, or is prior validation a documented/enforced precondition? Which actual callers can provide invalid indices?",
    "What minimum usable positive thickness, numerical resolution and disabled-self-contact policy are supported across CPU and GPU targets? Native handling of nonfinite grid input and any practical incident remain unobserved.",
    "How should manually authored mesh topology, rest lengths, masses and bend weights be correlated beyond the existing length/index/finite checks? Are partial geometry representations intended?",
    "How do related q622/q3296, F083, F003, existing tiny-mass and quantization questions map to unique ledger owners? Shared context or repair direction alone does not settle aliases.",
    "The direct public ShellMesh constructor can return before full validate; which external consumers rely on it and what empty/large geometry policy applies?"
  ],
